| Load the Bluetooth drivers before the desktop starts
| Raspberry Pi only (its DWCDriver is loaded): USBDriver 1.35 and the
| DWC host driver from the package.  Other boards keep their own USB stack.
Set Bluetooth$Pi 1
RMEnsure DWCDriver 0.00 Set Bluetooth$Pi 0
| A boot disc on USB (SCSI::) must not lose its drivers: leave them alone.
If "<Boot$Dir>" LEFT 5 = "SCSI:" Then Set Bluetooth$Pi 0
| A Pi 4 has its sockets on XHCI (VL805), where the DWC fix is not needed.
Set Bluetooth$XHCI 1
RMEnsure XHCIDriver 0.00 Set Bluetooth$XHCI 0
If "<Bluetooth$XHCI>" = "1" Then Set Bluetooth$Pi 0
Unset Bluetooth$XHCI
If "<Bluetooth$Pi>" = "1" Then IfThere BootResources:!Bluetooth.Modules.USBDriver Then RMEnsure USBDriver 1.35 RMLoad BootResources:!Bluetooth.Modules.USBDriver
If "<Bluetooth$Pi>" = "1" Then IfThere BootResources:!Bluetooth.Modules.DWCDriver Then RMEnsure DWCDriver 0.40 RMLoad BootResources:!Bluetooth.Modules.DWCDriver
Unset Bluetooth$Pi
IfThere BootResources:!Bluetooth.Modules.BTVoice Then RMEnsure BluetoothVoice 0.95 RMLoad BootResources:!Bluetooth.Modules.BTVoice
